{"name":"Getaway","hex":"#ac9b7b","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"getaway","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A means of escape.","The effecting of an escape."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Pertaining to an escape, as in a vehicle or plans."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/getaway"}],"entries":[{"title":"Crime scene getaway","blocks":[{"text":"A crime scene getaway is the act of departing from the location where one has committed a crime. It is an act that the offender(s) may or may not have planned in detail, resulting in a variety of outcomes. A crime scene is the \"location of a crime; especially one at which forensic evidence is collected in a controlled manner.\" The \"getaway\" is any escape by a perpetrator from that scene, which may have been witnessed by eyewitnesses or law enforcement."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/78/Teerahertz_near-field_array_for_%CE%BCm-scale_surface_imaging_%28cropped%29.png/330px-Teerahertz_near-field_array_for_%CE%BCm-scale_surface_imaging_%28cropped%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crime_scene_getaway","wikidata":"Q5185441"},{"title":"Vacation","blocks":[{"text":"A vacation or holiday is either a leave of absence from a regular job or school or an instance of leisure travel away from home. People often take a vacation during specific holiday observances or for specific festivals or celebrations. Vacations are often spent with friends or family. Vacations may include a specific trip or journey, usually for the purpose of recreation or tourism."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/42/Vacation_Village_at_Weston_Pool%2C_Weston%2C_Florida_February_24%2C_2022_B.jpg/330px-Vacation_Village_at_Weston_Pool%2C_Weston%2C_Florida_February_24%2C_2022_B.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vacation","wikidata":"Q116213"},{"title":"Getaway (TV series)","blocks":[{"text":"Getaway is Australia's longest-running travel and lifestyle television program. Debuting on 14 May 1992 in a Thursday 7:30 pm time slot, it is broadcast on the Nine Network and TLC. Its main competitor was The Great Outdoors on the Seven Network until 2009."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Getaway_(TV_series)","wikidata":"Q10847311"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d9/Days-of-vacation-and-holidays.png/500px-Days-of-vacation-and-holidays.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d9/Days-of-vacation-and-holidays.png/1280px-Days-of-vacation-and-holidays.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d9/Days-of-vacation-and-holidays.png/500px-Days-of-vacation-and-holidays.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Average number of vacation days over time in various countries","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADays-of-vacation-and-holidays.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/41/Vacation_research_design.jpg/500px-Vacation_research_design.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/41/Vacation_research_design.jpg/1280px-Vacation_research_design.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/41/Vacation_research_design.jpg/500px-Vacation_research_design.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Vacation research design","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AVacation_research_design.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/com